Package: remote
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-pil, python3-tk, xclip, ffmpeg
Recommends: tailscale, v4l2loopback-dkms
Maintainer: Remote <noreply@example.com>
Description: AnyDesk-style remote desktop for Linux over Tailscale
 Remote lets you control a Linux machine from your phone or another
 computer over a Tailscale network (WireGuard-encrypted P2P). The host
 streams its screen as compressed frames and injects the viewer's
 mouse/keyboard input, gated by a password challenge-response handshake
 and trust-on-first-use device pairing.
 .
 v1.0.0 host agent: modular host/ package (capture, input, net, auth,
 files, clipboard, audio, terminal, monitor, security, updater, tray,
 plugins); X11 capture with Wayland degrade-via-portal; adaptive
 FPS/bitrate from measured RTT; Tailscale integrated via the
 yourremote-network-setup wizard; pairing with YR-XXXX-XXXX device IDs,
 single-use codes and QR; per-device permission flags enforced
 fail-closed; clipboard images; real audio engine (PulseAudio/PipeWire);
 allowlisted app launcher and system commands (never a raw shell);
 JSON-lines logging with rotation; hardened systemd unit running as the
 unprivileged yourremote user; update checker against GitHub releases;
 plugin registry; policy.conf privacy toggles; TUI settings editor.
 .
 The viewer is a native Android app, distributed as an APK via GitHub
 Releases (see https://github.com/kilomene/Remote).
